# Wanted (IDEAS I20 b, I25 a; QUESTIONS Q29, 3; board 0.4). Fails until it is answered; then it moves up into collab/scenarios.
# Story: a person moves windows about as on any Mac. Near a screen edge, near another window: nothing of Arbor's shows and nothing
# docks. Holding ⌘ while dragging asks Arbor. macOS's own tiling is off here, so that the edges would be Arbor's to take.
mac-tiling off
open Safari
open Notes
pick-up 101 2 400
expect preview none
let-go
expect floating 101
expect count docked 0
# With ⌘ held it docks there.
drag 101 2 400 cmd
expect docked 101
# Beside a docked window, plainly: it floats where it was let go.
pick-up 102 650 400
wait 1
expect preview none
let-go
expect floating 102
expect still 101
# A docked window dragged plainly comes out, at the size it had before Arbor sized it.
drag 101 700 300
expect floating 101
expect size 101 640x420
expect count docked 0
